    "durationMs": 189327,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `cmd/app/main.go` — entry point with `serve` and `migrate` modes, graceful shutdown, reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (nothing hard-coded), listens on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi v5.2.1 router with all four endpoints, strict JSON decoding, and validation\n- `internal/store/store.go` — pgx-based persistence with embedded, idempotent SQL migrations tracked in a `schema_migrations` table\n- `internal/store/migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — the `links` table (unique code, click counter, creation order)\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground; uses the prebuilt `bin/app` (rebuilds from vendored deps if missing, no network needed)\n- `README.md` — includes a \"Starting the server\" section plus API docs\n\n**Verified end-to-end against every requirement**\n- Create with generated and custom codes → `201` with `clicks: 0`, submitted URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged\n- Duplicate custom code → `409`; malformed JSON, missing/relative/hostless/ftp URLs, and codes of wrong length or characters → `422` — all with an `error` field\n- `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /links` (ascending creation order, `total`), unknown codes → `404` JSON\n- `GET /r/{code}` → `302` with exact `Location`, clicks increment exactly once per hit (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`, concurrency-safe)\n- Killed and restarted via `sh start.sh`: all links and click counts survived; DB left in a pristine empty state for the test suite\n\nOne note: pgx `@latest` requires Go 1.25, so I pinned `pgx v5.7.6`, the newest release compatible with the toolchain's Go 1.24.3."
  }
